  "articles": [
    {
      "title": "Devanagari without the line",
      "body": "<p>Gujarati grew out of the same family as Devanagari, and most letters are rounder versions of their Hindi cousins with the headline taken off: compare Gujarati <span lang=\"gu\">ક ગ મ</span> with Hindi <span lang=\"hi\">क ग म</span>. The script was long used for bookkeeping and letters, where writing fast without a line mattered more than looking formal.</p>\n<p>It works the same way: each consonant carries a short a, vowel signs attach to it, and the halant (<span lang=\"gu\">ક્</span>) removes the vowel.</p>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Look-alikes to watch",
      "body": "<p>Some pairs differ by one small stroke, and one letter looks like a digit:</p>\n<table>\n<tr><td lang=\"gu\">ઘ ધ</td><td>gha and dha: the same pair is easy to confuse in Hindi too</td></tr>\n<tr><td lang=\"gu\">પ ષ</td><td>pa and ṣa: ષ adds a stroke across the middle</td></tr>\n<tr><td lang=\"gu\">ર ૨</td><td>the letter ra and the digit 2</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>The chart puts the rows side by side so you can compare.</p>"
    },
    {
      "title": "Conjuncts and the half letter",
      "body": "<p>When two consonants meet with no vowel between them, the first usually loses its vertical bar and leans on the second, just as in Hindi:</p>\n<table>\n<tr><td lang=\"gu\">સ્ + ત = સ્ત</td><td>st, as in <span lang=\"gu\">નમસ્તે</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td lang=\"gu\">પ્ + ય = પ્ય</td><td>py, as in <span lang=\"gu\">પ્યાર</span> (love)</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>Letters without a bar, like <span lang=\"gu\">ડ ટ</span>, use the halant or stack instead: <span lang=\"gu\">ડ્ડ</span>. A <span lang=\"gu\">ર</span> before a consonant becomes a small hook on top, as in <span lang=\"gu\">ધર્મ</span>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "title": "The silent a",
      "body": "<p>Like Hindi, Gujarati drops the built-in a at the end of most words and often in the middle. <span lang=\"gu\">કમળ</span> is written ka-ma-ḷa but said kamaḷ, and <span lang=\"gu\">ઘર</span> is ghar.</p>"
    }
  ]
}
